# {{name}}

A Protoboard hardware project, started from the **wearable** template
(derived from the wearable-watch reference project). The system is described
in UHD (`@deltarobotics/uhd`); this project holds its sources, parts and CAD.

**Agents, start here.** Read this file, then the **build-a-project** skill
(`protoboard skills read build-a-project`; Skills, below): it gives the order of work from
`docs/brief.md` to a release, how far to take the design before asking
(concept, blocks, parts, definitions verified, schematic and PCB), and the
skill for each stage. The skills of this project's extensions are listed at
the end of this file; Skills, below, says how to read one. Before changing anything, and before describing
the project to anyone, run `protoboard doctor`, `protoboard check` and
`protoboard inspect`. The UHD reference is in
`node_modules/@deltarobotics/uhd/docs`, and how to write UHD is the
**uhd-authoring** skill, `node_modules/@deltarobotics/uhd/skills/uhd-authoring/SKILL.md`.

With Protoboard's MCP server connected (`protoboard-stack`, registered by
`protoboard agents setup` or the Protoboard settings page in VS Code), the
commands below are also tools:
call `project_status` first. The tools and the commands do the same thing.

The starting system is a BLE main board (Raytac MDBT50Q-1MV2 nRF52840 module,
3.0 V LDO, MCP73831 charger from USB-C, SWD pads) on a 200 mAh LP402030 cell
soldered to it by the cell's own leads. It checks with no errors and one
warning (`SRC_SINGLE_SOURCE`: the cell has one supplier, a risk to accept in
`docs/decisions.md` or to fix); it is not yet a product. Grow it from `docs/brief.md`.

## Layout

- `src/system.uhd.ts` — the top-level module (the root system): instances,
  links, harness assignments. It lives under `src/`; keep it there
- `src/boards/main/` — the main board: `main.uhd.ts` (components, nets, the
  board's edge), `lands.uhd.ts` (its copper pads), `circuit.config.ts` (the
  PCB: @protoboardai/ext-tscircuit; native design in `tscircuit/`, land patterns
  for the project's own pads in `tscircuit/footprints.json`, standard outputs
  in `out/`) and `firmware.config.ts` (Zephyr board files: @protoboardai/ext-zephyr,
  written to `zephyr/`)
- `src/enclosures/` — the case (none yet; see its README): @protoboardai/ext-enclosure-cad
- `src/harnesses/` — wire harnesses; each has a provider directory `<id>/`
  with its `cad.config.ts` (@protoboardai/ext-harness-cad)
- Parts, in three tiers:
  - `parts/catalog/<id>.json` + `parts/catalog/<id>/` — purchased parts from
    the Protoboard Cloud parts catalog with the files of their revision.
    Immutable; `parts/origins.json` pins them and `check` verifies them offline.
  - `parts/local/<id>.uhd.ts` — purchased parts researched in this project:
    the LP402030 cell (its CAD generated from the drawing by
    `parts/local/lipol-lp402030/lipol-lp402030.py`); evidence and
    verification in `parts/evidence/<id>/`
  - everything in `src/` — designed here
- `docs/brief.md` (the brief), `docs/product.json` (what the product is: summary, features,
  functions, requirements with how each is shown; the documents' first page reads it),
  `docs/decisions.md` (decisions, warnings dispositioned)
- `release/<version>/` — the Manufacturing Package (`protoboard release`; not committed)

